Package: countimp
Title: Multiple Imputation of Incomplete Count Data
Version: 3.0.1
Date: 2026-09-01
Authors@R: c(person("Kristian", "Kleinke", role = c("aut","cre","cph"),
    email = "mail@kristian-kleinke.de"),
    person("Jost", "Reinecke", role = c("aut", "ths"),
    email = "jost.reinecke@uni-bielefeld.de"))
Description: Multiple imputation of incomplete count data: ordinary,
    overdispersed, zero-inflated and hurdle counts, for single-level and
    two-level (clustered) data. Imputation models are specified either through
    an 'lme4'-style formula interface (formulas, family, draw) or, as before,
    through a predictor matrix and type codes. The imputation engine is
    contained in the package; 'mice' (Van Buuren and Groothuis-Oudshoorn,
    2011, <doi:10.18637/jss.v045.i03>) is optional and only needed for
    non-count imputation methods and for pooling. Methods follow Kleinke and
    Reinecke (2013, <doi:10.1111/stan.12009>).
Depends: R (>= 3.4.0)
Imports: glmmTMB, MASS, Matrix, nnet, stats, TMB, utils
